    <bpmn:process id="W_W721" name="W721. Store-Level Vendor Promodizer Floor Activity Coordination &amp; Compliance" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Vendor promodizer arrives at store for scheduled or unscheduled floor activity; or daily promodizer schedule review
Frequency: Daily (multiple promodizers per store)
Volume: ~2–5 promodizers active per store during promo periods; ~12,000–30,000 promodizer check-ins/month chain-wide (daily per the staffing cadence)
Owner: Department Supervisor
Participants: Vendor Promodizer, Department Supervisor, Store Manager, HR (promodizer compliance per W269)
Source: workflow W721 — Store-Level Vendor Promodizer Floor Activity Coordination &amp; Compliance</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W721_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W721_Lane1" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W721_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W721_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W721_Lane2" name="Department Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W721_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W721_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W721_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W721_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W721_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W721_Start4" name="Vendor promodizer arrives at store for scheduled or unscheduled floor activity; or daily…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W721_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W721_Task5" name="Daily promodizer schedule review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Daily promodizer schedule review: Store Manager or Department Supervisor reviews daily promodizer schedule: (a) system displays scheduled promodizer visits: vendor name, promodizer name, assigned department, approved activity (demonstration, shelf stocking, product sampling, inventory check), approved time window; (b) identify conflicts: multiple promodizers in same department, overlapping demo stations, promodizer scheduled during peak traffic when floor space is limited; (c) resolve conflicts by adjusting time slots or relocating activity areas
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Dept Supervisor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 10-15 min/day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W721_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W721_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W721_Task6" name="Promodizer check-in">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Promodizer check-in: upon arrival: (a) promodizer reports to customer service counter or department supervisor; (b) Department Supervisor verifies: (i) promodizer has valid BuildRight-issued ID/visitor badge per W581 vendor access management; (ii) promodizer is on the approved schedule; (iii) activity type matches approved activity for today; (c) if unscheduled visit: Store Manager decides to allow (if space available and activity is pre-approved type) or decline (redirect to vendor&#x27;s BuildRight account manager for scheduling); (d) issue floor access badge with time-limited validity
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 5 min per promodizer</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W721_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W721_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W721_Task7" name="Floor activity monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Floor activity monitoring: during promodizer activity: (a) Department Supervisor periodically checks promodizer activity (every 1-2 hours): (i) promodizer is in assigned area only; (ii) not interfering with customer shopping flow; (iii) not disparaging competing products; (iv) following BuildRight store rules: no loud music, no blocking aisles, no unauthorized promotional materials; (v) wearing required PPE if in paint/chemical department per W237; (b) if violations observed: (i) first offense: verbal warning and correction; (ii) repeated offense: ask promodizer to leave and report to vendor via W269; (iii) serious violation (customer harassment, theft, safety hazard): immediate removal and incident report per W471
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 5-10 min per check</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W721_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W721_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W721_Task8" name="Product demonstration coordination">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Product demonstration coordination: for promodizers conducting live product demonstrations: (a) Department Supervisor assigns demonstration area: not blocking main aisles, near relevant product section, with access to power outlet if needed; (b) verify demonstration materials are safe: no open flames, no hazardous chemicals without PPE, no food samples without sanitary compliance; (c) ensure demonstration does not create excessive noise or waste; (d) coordinate with cashier team if promodizer is offering special pricing or coupons that need POS setup per W523
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 10 min per demo setup</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W721_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W721_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W721_Task9" name="Promodizer check-out">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Promodizer check-out: at end of activity: (a) promodizer returns floor access badge; (b) Department Supervisor conducts brief debrief: (i) activity completed as planned?; (ii) any incidents or customer complaints?; (iii) any store property damage?; (iv) any inventory discrepancies noted?; (c) Department Supervisor logs visit completion in system with activity notes; (d) feedback sent to vendor via W269 promodizer management for performance tracking
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5 min per promodizer</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W721_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W721_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W721_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W721_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
